  "readmeFile": "Readme.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.3.0:\n- BREAKING: CarmelAccessToken.ToString() and string interpolation hide the token, so a header built from them sends \"Bearer CarmelAccessToken hidden\"; match CarmelAccessToken.Token to read it\n- BREAKING: redirects are not followed; a 3xx is a failure\n- BREAKING: parseWebhookResponse refuses a timestamp ahead by more than the tolerance, and a svix-signature entry that is not exactly v1,signature\n- FIXED: a returned Async runs again, re-sending the request; createCreditTransfer keeps its key and date\n- FIXED: createWebhookSubscription sends an Idempotency-Key derived from the endpoint and events, as Carmel documents for all POST requests\n- ADDED: createWebhookSubscriptionWithKey takes the id the key is built from\n- FIXED: createCreditTransfer and createWebhookSubscriptionWithKey refuse a blank id, which would share one Idempotency-Key\n- FIXED: docs state that a createCreditTransfer retry after Carmel's 24 hours can send a second ACH\n- CHANGED: approveCreditTransfer is documented as not safe to retry, as Carmel documents no key for PATCH; the library makes one attempt\n- FIXED: cancelling the Async cancels its HTTP request\n- FIXED: webhook signatures are compared in fixed time",
